KineticEnergyModel.

identity.
name- "Kinetic Energy Model";
description- "A causal framework for understanding motion, pressure, and energy through explicit relationships between potential, resistance, and displacement.";
status- "Active CE-OS engineering theory under computational development and physical evaluation";
authority- "This document defines the model as authored. Its claims are hypotheses, definitions, axioms, rules, and derived relationships within the model; inclusion here does not independently establish physical truth.";

purpose.
primary- "construct explicit causal chains rather than collapse system behavior into summary relationships";
engineering- "represent causal engineering systems so assumptions, resistance, displacement, domain transitions, predictions, measurements, and disagreements remain inspectable";
goal- "model how potential resolves through structure and determine experimentally where the model succeeds, fails, or remains incomplete";

foundation.
causality- "potential overcoming resistance produces displacement";
relationship- "p-r=d";
potential- "p";
resistance- "r";
displacement- "d";
energy- "energy is treated by this model as the relationship and resolution between causal potential and displacement rather than as an independently transported substance";
causal_chain- "identify potential, identify resistance, observe or calculate displacement";
explicitness- "potential, resistance, and displacement remain explicit rather than hidden behind summary metrics";

domains.
universal- "universal causal terms are defined under Engineering/qps/defs/KE/U.qps";
field_centric- "field-centric terms are defined under Engineering/qps/defs/KE/FC.qps";
mass_centric- "mass-centric terms are defined under Engineering/qps/defs/KE/MC.qps";
integrity- "domain-specific causal logic remains distinct";
bridge_rule- "no equation may combine Field-Centric and Mass-Centric terms unless a formal domain bridge is defined";
bridge_example- "Thermal -> Fluid -> Mechanical -> Electrical";
shared_terms- "universal causal terms such as potential, resistance, and displacement may participate across domains";

laws.

causality.
name- "Law of Causality";
claim- "all kinetic events are modeled as potential resolving against resistance into displacement";
relationship- "p-r=d";
interpretation- "potential exists as causal readiness under structural opposition and resolves as displacement when resistance permits";

mass_motion.
name- "Law of Mass-Motion Resolution";
claim- "mass-centric behavior is modeled using force, acceleration, inertia, momentum, resistance, and impact relationships";
force_relation- "f=ma";
momentum_relation- "mv";
impact_relation- "mv-r=f_impact";
source_extended_relation- "p*a*m-r=v*m-r=f_impact";
status- "model claim requiring explicit dimensional and experimental treatment before predictive use";

principles.

relationships.
rule- "relationships are primary";
description- "KE relationships describe causal structure. Predictive behavior belongs to explicitly executable domain models with stated assumptions.";

resolution.
rule- "model resolution rather than hide causal transitions";
description- "models must show how a causal state changes through resistance and displacement rather than relying solely on aggregate outcome accounting";

explicit_terms.
rule- "causal terms remain explicit";
description- "potential, resistance, and displacement may not be silently omitted when they are part of the modeled causal relationship";

clarity.
rule- "clarity is law";
description- "variables, constants, assumptions, domains, and bridges must be explicitly identified";

definitions.
rule- "definitions are sacred";
description- "terms used by axioms and theorems require standalone scoped definitions";

axioms.
rule- "axioms are foundational model claims";
description- "an axiom must be represented as a primitive claim of this model rather than silently derived from another claim";

theorems.
rule- "theorems are derived";
description- "derived claims must trace to the definitions, axioms, relationships, and assumptions from which they follow";

causal_chains.
rule- "causal chains are foundational";
description- "systems are represented as sequences of explicit causal events rather than collapsed abstractions";

resistance.
rule- "resistance is explicit";
description- "resistance is accounted for as a causal interaction and is not assigned an assumed value merely to close an equation";

geometry.
rule- "geometry may alter causal conditions";
description- "structure and geometry may change potential, resistance, displacement, routing, concentration, or domain coupling and therefore belong in the causal model";

measurement.
rule- "prediction and measurement remain distinct";
description- "a calculated or simulated result is not a measured physical result";

validation.
rule- "physical claims remain falsifiable";
description- "the model must permit experimental evidence to support, contradict, constrain, or expose missing relationships";

axiom_0.
name- "Thermal Genesis";
claim- "the model proposes primordial cold causal retraction preceding thermal expression";
ether- "Ether is proposed as a continuous structural substrate responsive to causal tension";
transition- "thermal expression and Hydrogen formation are proposed to arise when structural resistance reaches a transition threshold";
consequence- "motion is not defined as requiring heat";
status- "foundational cosmological hypothesis";

axiom_1.
name- "Field Coexistence and Influence";
claim- "fields are modeled as distinct causal structures that may coexist and influence one another without being reduced to one another";
coexistence- "fields may share space while retaining distinct structure";
influence- "one field may modify the potential, resistance, or displacement conditions of another";
ether_clause- "field resolution is modeled through Ether while Ether itself is not classified as a field";
status- "foundational field-model hypothesis";

axiom_2.
name- "Field Alignment / Magnetic Persistence";
claim- "persistent magnetic behavior is modeled as stable repeating field geometry";
persistence- "resistance is proposed to be integrated into stable field structure rather than eliminated";
interaction- "magnetic fields may alter resistance conditions in electrical and mechanical interactions";
status- "field-model hypothesis";

axiom_3.
name- "Stellar Genesis";
claim- "stellar formation is modeled as sustained causal retraction, condensation, thermal displacement, pressure accumulation, and eventual collapse when outward resolution fails";
refrigerant_effect- "outward thermal displacement is proposed to permit deeper central compression";
collapse- "Thermal Inversion Collapse is proposed as the transition into fusion";
status- "cosmological hypothesis";

axiom_4.
name- "Reactive Threshold";
claim- "chemical reaction is modeled as structural field reconfiguration after stored potential exceeds structural resistance";
activation- "external excitation or internal rearrangement may raise potential or lower resistance until threshold crossing";
catalyst- "a catalyst lowers resistance without supplying the modeled potential";
relationship- "p-r>0";
status- "chemical-model hypothesis";

axiom_5.
name- "Plasma Threshold";
claim- "plasma is modeled as a structurally unstable, conductive, field-reactive state produced under extreme thermal and pressure excitation";
relation_to_reaction- "stellar plasma and fusion are modeled as threshold behavior related to Reactive Threshold";
status- "plasma-model hypothesis";

axiom_6.
name- "Inductive Propagation";
claim- "electromagnetic propagation is modeled as recursive field excitation through Ether";
mechanism- "electric and magnetic states recursively induce changes in one another";
termination- "propagation ceases or changes when resistance exceeds potential, resolution completes, or geometry constrains propagation";
relationship- "p-r=d";
status- "electromagnetic propagation hypothesis";

axiom_7.
name- "Electric Conduction";
claim- "electrical current is modeled as displacement of electric potential through structured mass rather than bulk electron transport";
DC- "DC is modeled as directionally sustained field displacement";
AC- "AC is modeled as cyclic field realignment";
relationship- "p-r=d_field";
status- "electrical-model hypothesis";

axiom_8.
name- "Gravity";
claim- "gravity is modeled as continuous causal field pressure rather than acceleration itself";
source_gravity_expression- "g=9.8 m/s";
source_relation- "i/r=g";
interaction- "acceleration of mass is treated as an effect occurring when resistance conditions permit displacement";
ether- "gravity is proposed as an interaction with Ether / zero-point structure";
status- "gravity-model hypothesis requiring dimensional and experimental resolution";

axiom_9.
name- "Abundance / Tesla Axiom";
claim- "the model proposes that potential is continuously available wherever field structure exists and that energy is resolved rather than consumed";
geometry- "scarcity of usable expression is attributed to resistance and geometry";
status- "foundational hypothesis";

axiom_10.
name- "Energy";
claim- "energy is the conditional relationship between causal tension and displacement";
relationship- "p-r=d";
potential- "potential is modeled as unresolved causal displacement under opposition";
displacement- "displacement is modeled as resolved potential";
boundary- "when resistance is greater than or equal to potential, sustained displacement does not occur";
status- "foundational model definition and hypothesis";

axiom_11.
name- "Fire";
claim- "fire is modeled as the field-level resolution region of a chemical reaction in which several causal outputs occur simultaneously";
inputs- "fuel stored potential, oxidizer/environmental resistance conditions, and sufficient excitation";
outputs- "thermal excitation, electromagnetic emission, and fluid expansion";
relationship- "P_chem-R_env=D_thermal+D_EM+D_fluid_ambient";
status- "multidomain reaction hypothesis";

applications.
engineering- "turbines, motors, pumps, generators, hydraulic systems, power conversion, and other engineered causal systems";
field_theory- "field interactions including magnetic, electromagnetic, thermal, and gravitational hypotheses";
education- "explicit causal decomposition of physical relationships";
translation- "systems that bridge thermal, fluid, mechanical, and electrical domains";
HEV- "Hydraulic Electric System modeling and experiment design";

research_direction.
statement- "More potential, more displacement";
amplifying_potential- "investigate whether geometry or causal conditions can increase usable potential at a downstream interaction without hiding the source or resistance";
resistance_reduction- "identify and reduce actual resistance mechanisms where possible";
balance- "compare potential, resistance, and displacement explicitly";

unresolved.

energy_constant.
claim- "the source material proposes a universal conversion constant between potential and displacement called the Energy Constant";
symbol- "e";
status- "unresolved hypothesis";

mass_centric_energy_constant_form.
source_model_md- "(f-r)e=mv";
source_model_yaml- "(f-r)e=v";
status- "source disagreement preserved; neither form is canonical until resolved";

prediction_scope.
source_model_md- "Kinetic Energy equations express relationships, not predictions";
source_model_yaml- "Kinetic Energy equations express relationships, not predictions; Mass-centric and field-centric systems do model predictions";
resolution- "the base causal relationship is descriptive; prediction requires an executable domain model with explicit assumptions";
status- "working interpretation; preserve source distinction until formally accepted";

linear_algebra.
source_rule- "all relationships must resolve along a single dimension of causal flow; tensors, vector fields, and probabilistic functions are excluded from core logic";
status- "legacy construction constraint requiring review against current Engineering geometry and simulation requirements";

efficiency.
legacy_usage- "older source prose refers to efficiency as a system constraint";
current_rule- "efficiency is not a primitive causal input";
derivation- "efficiency may be calculated afterward from explicit input/output states and actual loss mechanisms";
status- "current Engineering interpretation";

evidence.
requirement- "claims must be distinguishable from measurements";
apparatus- "physical apparatus supplies measurements";
comparison- "predicted and measured states remain separate";
difference- "differences between predicted and measured states must remain inspectable";
failure_modes- "missing model, implementation error, measurement error, contradicted hypothesis, supported hypothesis, or unresolved evidence";

provenance.
source_readme- "Engineering/qps/docs/README.md";
source_model_md- "Engineering/qps/docs/model.md";
source_model_yaml- "Engineering/qps/docs/model.yaml";
source_axioms- "Engineering/qps/docs/axioms.md";
definition_universal- "Engineering/qps/defs/KE/U.qps";
definition_field- "Engineering/qps/defs/KE/FC.qps";
definition_mass- "Engineering/qps/defs/KE/MC.qps";
policy- "source disagreements and unresolved claims are retained explicitly rather than silently overwritten";
